--- body ---
## Context

Observed across all four executors and all four gaze runs of the 2026-10-02
raid on 0853/0937/0979/1014 (Vibe runtime, PRs #1129-#1132). Subagent
sessions spawned via the runtime's agent connector do not expose the agent
connector themselves: tools.agent is absent in every child session. Every
skill that asks a child to spawn reviewer seats (hunt step 11's review-pr,
gaze phases 2-4/6) therefore fails its panel in child sessions.

Three of four executors reported PANEL-INTEGRITY: DEGRADED with all
perspectives "no report" and escalated; the fourth (PR #1129's executor)
instead ran its three reviewers as detached headless `claude -p` processes
pinned read-only to the review worktree, polled by artifact — and got a full
3/3 panel. All four gaze orchestrators then independently rediscovered the
same detached-CLI pattern to run their batteries; two of them mis-launched it
first (word-split deny rules, default-opus model instead of the intended
sonnet) and had to relaunch. The pattern works; it is just undocumented, so
every session pays its own discovery and first-launch failures.

## Actions

1. Document the detached-seat pattern where the spawn contract fails: one
   section in skills/review-pr/SKILL.md (and cross-referenced from gaze's
   reviewer-spawn phase) stating the substitution — headless CLI process per
   seat, prompt embedding the seat's contract, cwd/--add-dir pinned to the
   review worktree, read-only rails restated in the prompt, completion
   observed by artifact polling, never by trusting the spawn's exit status
   (memory: raid-1008 spawn-under-cap recorded spawn returning success while
   the child never registered).
2. Pin the quoting discipline (deny-rules passed as one string) and the
   model-pinning note (per-seat model selection may not be enforceable
   through the detached CLI on every runtime — record the limitation
   instead of silently running a different model).

## Test

A doc-pin test asserting the pattern section exists and names its load
-bearing elements (detached CLI, artifact polling, read-only rails,
spawn-success-not-trust), in the established doc-pin style
(cf. tests/test_pi_provider_assertion_rule.py).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The substitution pattern is documented in the review-pr skill with its
      failure modes, so a child session without tools.agent runs its panel
      instead of reporting DEGRADED
- [ ] A doc-pin test keeps the section from drifting

## Invariants

- Fail-open stays for seats; nothing here makes a seat blocking.
- A seat that cannot run is recorded as no-report with PANEL-INTEGRITY
  status, never simulated (that held in all eight runs).
